WEBVTT

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.580
Did you go anywhere during
our extended days off?

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.040
Nah.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.450
Hello, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.950
Heya!

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.040
Hello. Where's the president?

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.910
She's snoring away in the club room.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.160
I don't think she's doing anything today.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.000
Oh, yeah.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.870
I had something to ask you, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.500
I found this in my grandpa's fishing supplies.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.620
It looked a bit strange,
so I was curious about it.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.660
Oh, that.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.950
This is called a <i>burakuri </i>rig
and it's a rig used to catch rockfish.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:18.450
Rockfish?

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.000
Around here, you could probably catch
scorpionfish and red spotted groupers.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.750
They live in the gaps between the
breakwater's blocks, rocks, and reefs.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.330
You drop your rig into those gaps and fish.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:34.500
That's called <i>burakuri </i>fishing,
or light rock fishing.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.870
Wow...

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.160
You catch them right under the breakwater,

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.160
so you don't even need to
cast your line. It's really casual.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.870
Wow, that sounds fun!

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.830
My first time fishing
was light rock fishing, too.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.410
You don't know what gaps the fish are in,

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:53.250
so it's exciting when you
put your rig into the gaps.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.370
Once you catch one, you need
to reel them up immediately,

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.500
or they may drag your line
down so you have to cut it...

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.330
But if you move too fast,
you might lose your rig.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.290
But all that makes it even more fun!

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.290
There's all kinds of <i>burakuri </i>fishing.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.250
For the breakwater blocks,

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:09.750
you need to let your rig get
super down there, and...

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.950
A-Anyway, it's a lot of fun.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.450
We could tell!

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.410
Light rock fishin' sounds good.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:25.120
--President.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:25.830
--Hey, she's up.
--President.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.790
It's great for beginners, and
I want some scorpies miso soup.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.950
Scorpies?

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.250
She means scorpionfish.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.950
Put it in miso soup and
it turns out super delicious!

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.080
Let's do some light rock fishing!

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.750
Ohno, make sure ya show Tsurugi the ropes.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.750
You're not going to do anything, are you?

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:47.830
Th-Then, let's catch some delicious scorpies.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.870
--Yeah!
--Scorpies!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.000
Right under here.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.870
Be careful so you don't fall.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.450
Okay.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:02.830
So many rocks down there.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:05.660
There are rockfish somewhere in those gaps.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.160
Huh? This close?

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.290
It's really shallow.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.290
They're there.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:15.700
Even in low tide, as long as there's
still water, they're definitely there.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.290
Also, they're some in those
breakwater blocks over there.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.620
Oh, that really rocky area.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:22.910
I see.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:26.330
You're probably not athletic
enough for that area though.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.660
Why?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.250
Because you move around on top of those blocks.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.580
Sometimes, you even have to jump.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.580
Knowing your athletic skills,
you'll probably fall and get super hurt.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.290
Worst case scenario, you may even drown.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.620
Drown?!

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:44.040
It's best for people with
no athletic skills to just stay away.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.200
The breakwater is low over here
and there's plenty of room,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.910
so it's pretty safe.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:52.580
You thought all that through for me?

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.870
Way to go, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>!

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:59.040
Also, put this on, just in case.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.500
Huh? But isn't this yours, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>?

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.000
Don't worry. I'll be careful so I won't fall.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.040
No.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.500
It's dangerous if you get too
absorbed into light rock fishing,

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.370
so this is just in case.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.870
O-Okay...

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.620
What's so funny?

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:23.450
Well, ya see, when
Ohno was in grade school...

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.750
"Menacing"

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.500
Never mind... Forget I said anythin'...

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:34.870
Oh, right. I've got Sayaka
gettin' us more life jackets.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.950
We should be gettin' them soon.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:41.660
Thank goodness. I'm not
a great swimmer, so that'll help.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:46.250
I'm totally fine without one.
I'm an awesome swimmer.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.950
Yer type's the kind that drowns first.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.120
Never forget how scary the ocean is.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.700
Right, Ohno?

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.790
You're always cautious since you're
always wearing one, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.660
You can never be too prepared.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.370
You're so amazing, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:14.540
It's so nice that you just have
to tie on a <i>burakuri </i>for the rig.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:18.160
It's perfect for beginners.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.500
There must be some reason
it's shaped like this, right?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.700
Cone-shaped weights don't
get caught on rocks as much

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.790
and get to the bottom easier.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.000
The reason there's little
space between the weight and hook

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.790
is so it won't catch on things.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:34.830
Wow... Someone really thought this through.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.080
Oh, what kind of bait do we use?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:40.040
Worms are the best, but...

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.830
W-W-W-W-Worms?!

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.790
Hina!

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:47.750
So worms...

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.540
...look like this!

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.620
I can't. I can't. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
I'm done for today. Thank you very much.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:56.700
There, there.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.500
That bad?

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.870
It's okay.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.250
We'll use sliced squid today.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.660
Th-Thank goodness.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.950
Weave it on.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.870
Like this?

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.790
Yes.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:15.080
Okay, I'm gonna catch one!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.870
I wonder where I should drop it.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:25.620
I think there's one down here.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.290
Once you hit the bottom,

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:35.540
bounce it up and down a
couple times to attract the fish.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:36.660
Okay.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.700
I'm not getting anything.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:44.910
Then let's try another hole.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.790
Already?

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:49.910
Scorpies latch on immediately if they're around.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:51.580
Huh...

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:55.000
--Hup!

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:55.370
--B-Be careful...
--Hup!

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:56.830
--B-Be careful...

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.120
Okay.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.290
It's sort of exciting waiting to get a hit.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.910
Yes. That's a lot of fun.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.660
I'm not having much luck.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.410
They might've all been snatched up
during the extended holiday.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.540
There are only so many holes
they'll make their homes in.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:38.540
I see. Maybe they're all vacant now.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.120
In that case...

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.870
Your best bet are these holes closest
to the wall that people usually ignore.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:48.700
What? Those are really narrow, though.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.620
Are they really in there?

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.540
That's exactly why though.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:55.910
It's usually surprisingly roomy inside.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.370
Rockfish love spaces like that.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:01.410
But they're hard to aim for
since they're so narrow.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.450
Okay, I'll give it a try!

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:08.500
I'm really good at getting
thread into needle holes.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.450
Good job, me.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.700
Reel it in all at once
so they can't dive deeper.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.450
O-Okay!

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:31.540
There really was one!

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:37.040
Scorpy? Is that a scorpy?

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.790
It sure is. It's pretty big, too!

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:43.120
That's awesome, Hina!

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:46.160
I did it!

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.250
It's red!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.700
Colorful, right?

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.160
Its eyes, fins, and mouth are so big!

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:52.000
Right?

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.580
It's definitely cuter than a flathead.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.540
I-It's cute?

00:09:56.540 --> 00:10:00.160
H-How do I...?

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:03.290
If you touch it with your bare hands,
it's really prickly, so it'll hurt. Be careful!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.540
Huh? Then how am I supposed to get the hook off?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:08.950
With this!

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:10.620
This?

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:12.160
Grasp!

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:16.450
This is how you hold a scorpy. Easy, right?

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:17.700
Here, give it a try.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:19.450
I-I'm scared!

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:24.160
You're able to gut fish now,
so this should be easy!

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.950
Don't keep the poor thing waiting forever.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.700
Will it bite? Hey, it won't bite, will it?

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:33.040
Don't worry, you'll be fine.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:35.790
Make sure you hold on tight. They flail.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.250
Your face, your face... Look at your face.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.450
I-I got it!

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.410
Hey, good job.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.040
Let's get a photo.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:51.870
Forget that! Just get me the cooler! Hurry!

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:54.750
Go put it in yourself.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.950
That was so scary...

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:02.450
If yer that scared, just use some tongs.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:05.870
Why didn't you tell me you had that?!

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.330
Looks like we got one for each of us.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.450
Yeah!

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.120
Well, how was light rock fishing, Hina?

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.040
It was a lot of fun!

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:22.000
Scorpies pull a lot harder than
the horsies and I sorta like it!

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.830
I'd love to do this again!

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:24.910
Yes.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:28.540
But let's wait until we get our life jackets.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.120
It's fine that you like doing this,

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.370
but it's really dangerous if you get
so absorbed you don't see anything else.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:39.120
Did something happen to you when
you were light rock fishing, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>?

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:42.290
You seem a bit weird today.

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:45.200
Ohno, just tell them already.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.540
So they don't make the same mistake.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:57.700
When I first went light rock fishing
with my father, I got too absorbed, and...

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:00.700
You fell into the ocean?!

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:05.700
I almost drowned. I was lucky
my dad saved me, but...

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:09.580
Ever since, I always wear a life jacket.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.370
Oh...

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.540
And ya can't swim since.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.040
You can't swim?

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:21.040
I would've never guessed. You look so athletic.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:24.910
You seem so perfect, yet you can't swim...
Actually, that's also sorta perfect.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:28.370
Th-The ocean is really scary, so be careful...

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:31.750
We will! We understand now!

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:38.000
"Report 07"
"'Light Rock Fishing'"

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:41.950
It finally stopped raining.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:45.000
I know it's the rainy season,
but it really was nonstop.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.330
Let's go fishing together tomorrow.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:48.790
What?

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:51.410
Even I'm gonna study over the weekend.

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:54.330
Huh? Study? Why?

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.250
Well, we've got midterms starting Monday.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:56.580
"Midterms"
Well, we've got midterms starting Monday.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.580
"Midterms"
What?!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:57.870
What?!

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.910
Wait, did you forget?

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.620
I did...

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:08.410
Wh-Wh-Wh-What should I do?!
I haven't studied at all!

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:11.870
We didn't have club because all of the rain.
What were you doing at home?

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:15.540
I spent all my time making plushies!

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:20.200
Then let's study together at my place tomorrow.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.910
I'll probably slack if I study alone.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:26.450
Really? With you?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.660
You think I'm stupid, don't you?!

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:36.750
I'll have you know I was in the top ten
of my class for academics in middle school.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:37.830
What?!

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.410
Never mind, then. I'll study on my own.

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:45.000
I-I'll come over! Please let me come over!

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.040
It's finally sunny.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:47.750
"Western Cuisine Café Hodaka"
It's finally sunny.

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:48.660
"Western Cuisine Café Hodaka"

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:52.330
Oh, they run a Western cuisine restaurant.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:55.000
H-Hello...

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:04.080
Hello?

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:06.790
I wonder if I should've come in from here.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.370
Excuse me, miss, but we're not open yet.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:14.830
We can't have you just barge in like that.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.290
Just kidding.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.500
Wait, why're you so frozen?

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.200
Glasses...

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:27.200
Who cares? They're more comfortable sometimes.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.330
Do you usually wear contacts?

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:30.290
Yeah.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:32.500
Oh.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.790
Wait, is that you, Hina?

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:40.870
Y-Yes, it is. Hello.

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:43.790
My goodness! You've grown so much!

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:47.200
It's been so long! Do you remember me?

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.870
Um, I... No, I'm sorry...

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:52.950
Well, I can't blame you. You were really little.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.330
So you're the friend who's coming over today.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.750
I'm so happy you're going to
the same high school as Natsumi!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.790
She's a bit loud, but
I hope you'll bear with her.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:04.700
Oh, sure. Natsumi's actually
been helping me out a lot.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:08.370
U-Um, this isn't much,
but this is from my mother.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:11.790
Oh, how nice! Are they snacks?

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:14.540
I'll bring some up later
when I bring you girls some tea.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:18.410
Oh, how is your mom?
I haven't talked to her in so long...

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:22.620
That's enough of that!
And you're way louder than I am!

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:26.870
What? It's been ages since
I've seen her! Let me talk to her!

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:28.540
Hina, hurry and come in.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.870
Th-Thanks for having me.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:34.250
Make sure you come down for lunch!

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.120
I'll make you something yummy!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:38.580
Thank you!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.660
Honestly...

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:42.330
I can definitely tell you're related.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.660
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:48.250
It reminded me of when we were reunited.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:50.410
You guys are like twins!

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:55.950
It's not big, but make yourself at home.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.330
Just sit wherever you want. Is barley tea okay?

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.200
Sure, thanks.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:04.660
So you share a room with your younger brother?

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:08.290
Yup. He's out playing today,
so don't worry about him.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:20.660
What? Did you see something unusual?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:27.790
No, it's just I've never really been
to a friend's house, so this is all new.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.290
Hina...

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:34.370
Wait, what? Don't look at me like that!

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:34.750
"Arithmetic 1"

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:37.370
"Arithmetic 1"
Oh, you totally made me think...

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:41.540
Jeez, even I had friends.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:42.790
Ah...

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:45.250
Not that many, though.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:51.290
So, Hina...

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:53.250
About these friends...

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:56.790
Oh, there's a girl named Mako
who was in my class in middle school.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:17:01.120
She liked handicrafts, too,
so we became pretty close.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.950
I see. You bonded over your hobbies.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:09.450
Yeah. She'd come over on our
days off to make plushies and stuff.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:11.700
Huh...

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:16.620
She'd always come over to my place,
so I rarely went over to hers!

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:18.620
That's what I meant earlier!

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.910
Okay, jeez. Let's get started.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.160
"Arithmetic 1"
Okay, jeez. Let's get started.

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.700
I can't... I don't get it at all.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:36.830
Which one?

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.870
For this, you take this formula and...

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.370
Oh, I see.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:56.830
Correct.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:59.000
Yay!

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:03.410
Look at you two, studying hard.

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:05.870
Come down for some lunch
before it gets too crowded.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:09.790
It's already lunchtime? It went by so fast.

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:12.870
It's nice being able to
concentrate since it's the two of us.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:18.660
I may be biased, but our
Napolitan spaghetti's pretty great.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.620
It looks amazing...

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.000
Thank you so much for lunch.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.870
Don't even worry about it! Just eat up.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.620
The plate's hot though, so be careful.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.500
It's so good!

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:40.660
Right?

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:43.910
Thank you for the food! It was delicious!

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:47.080
I'm glad you liked it.
Good luck with your studies.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.830
Thank you.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.410
Man, I'm so done.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:57.910
Yeah...

00:18:57.910 --> 00:19:00.370
It's so sunny outside.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.120
Must be the sun break during the rainy season.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.580
What's the weather tomorrow?

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.750
Rain, 100% chance.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:11.700
I see. Rain, huh?

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:14.080
Yup. Rain.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.830
Hey, what's this? A horse mackerel?

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:23.290
It's even got scales.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:26.000
Oh, that?

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.040
Let me see it for a sec.

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:33.950
And just like that, prepping is all done.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:40.660
What the heck?! Wow!

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:41.870
Is this from back then?

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:46.620
Yeah. I wanted to get used to fish a bit more.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.450
Wait, you were making this?
This is why you weren't studying?

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:55.040
Once I started, I couldn't stop.
I totally forgot about the tests.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.080
Amazing...

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:57.750
R-Really?

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.410
You're so amazingly dumb.

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:01.080
Wha...?!

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.700
But this is impressive.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:06.790
"Look, Mako! You can take its guts out"

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:09.540
"Look, Mako! You can take its guts out"
Mako was surprised when
I sent her a picture of it.

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.370
"Look, Mako! You can take its guts out"
Yeah, I'm sure she was.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:11.700
Yeah, I'm sure she was.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:14.580
She was even more surprised
when I told her I was fishing.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:23.160
This is great. I want one, too.

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.160
Then I'll make you one!

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:26.700
Sure.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:31.120
Actually... I'd like to make one myself.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:34.080
Then I'll show you how to make one next time!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.000
Really?

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.660
Yeah, of course! Leave it to me!

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:42.870
I think this is too complicated to start with,
so maybe something a bit simpler.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.950
What? But this is really easy, though.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:48.080
It's definitely complicated.
Way too complicated.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:49.620
You think so?

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:53.500
I'm not great with my hands, so
something for beginners would be better.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:57.080
Oh, then there's something
really easy you can make with felt,

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.330
so let's make that.

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:01.580
Sure. But after our tests are done.

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:06.580
Let's do some knitting, too.
I've got plenty of yarn at home.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.330
I might not be ready for that just yet...

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.330
Wait. Yarn...

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.250
Hina, look at this.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:16.330
"I tried some light tackle fishing with yarn!"

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.330
"Yarn bait"
"Will I catch anything?"

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.330
"Fishing start"

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:23.200
Wow, he actually caught one.

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:25.620
Right? Those things eat anything.

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:27.540
You won't have to worry
about paying much for bait then.

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:28.950
Hey, he got another one.

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:29.250
"Caught a 2nd one!"
Hey, he got another one.

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:30.580
"Caught a 2nd one!"
That seems fun.

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:31.200
"Caught a 2nd one!"
Right?

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:31.950
Right?

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:42.410
I wanna try.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.660
Huh?

00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:45.910
Let's go!

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:47.620
I'll go bring some yarn!

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:50.250
I have some fishing rods at my place,
so don't worry about that!

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:51.580
Okay!

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:55.080
We're having some scorpy miso soup tonight!

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:58.160
Today's haiku...

00:21:58.160 --> 00:21:59.750
"Life jackets are great.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.330
Life jackets can save your life,

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:03.040
and also your soul."

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:04.540
Makoto.
